          "ocr_text": "May 22\nS- Becl the following night the Lord stood by him and said \"Be of good cheer Paul for as you have testified for me in Jerusalem so you must also bear witness at Rome.\" Acts 23:11\n\nO- Interesting that Paul shared this with Luke. Luke would hear of Paul's vision then record all the obstacles contrary to that vision. 40 days taking an oath. Nephew hearing plot Paul. believed it kid commanded 470 others to get Paul. This must have built Luke's faith that when Jesus says \"Paul will suffer many things in my name\". They would need to have artist in a God who is able to deliver and will at some times, but who has to power to deliver and its His will to not do so at other times.\n\nA- I need to have trust in God. Not just in His power to deliver me, but also in his willingness to allow girls not knowing that it all God and His timing frame will somehow extend beyond my life.\n\nP- God help me to just in you during both good and bad times knowing you love me and see all things beyond the scope of my understanding.\n\nMay 23\nS- Peter replied \"Repent and be baptized everyone of you in the name of Jesus Christ for the forgiveness of sins. And you will receive the gift of the Holy Spirit. The promise is for you and your children and for all who are far off for all whom the Lord our God will call.\" Acts 2:38,39\n\nO- Repentance looks different for every person who believes on Jesus as Savior. Water washed Paul. Ananias gave money. Paul preached Peter did fishing. He promise is for my kids.\n\nA- What does repentance look like for me? I don't know yet. I feel like Peter who decided Jesus and went Back to Fishing. How do I return?\n\nP- Jesus please find me. Encounter me again. Draw me and make me whole.",
