          "ocr_text": "May 5\nS- Know your enemies in that you may be sons of your Father for all things that evil and the good and the rains rain on the just and the unjust. If you love these you love you what reward have you? Do not even tax collectors do the same? Matt 5:45, uc\n\nO- Jesus tells us to be like his Father and His sons. As we forgive because like Christ and souls of God. He forgives without condition. When we bless all us He blesses because we look like Him.\n\nA- I will forgive and bless others. because I want to look like my Father\n\nP- God give me grace to live like you. Love like you. Lead like you everyday.\n\nMay 4\nS- I indeed baptize you with water unto repentance but He who comes after me will baptize you with Holy Spirit and His winnowing Fan is in his Hand and He will thoroughly clean out His threshing Floor and gather His wheat into the barn but He will burn up the chaff with unquenchable fire. Matt 3:11,E\n\nO- John told that Jesus would baptize with the Holy Spirit. That He would separate the wheat and chaff. This may be why Jesus is not recorded at baptizing in water. He baptizes with fire/ Holy Spirit.\n\nA- I want to be baptized into Christ through water- repentance and by Jesus- w/ Holy Spirit and Fire.\n\nP- God please baptize me everyday with your spirit/and fire to be a witness through answered prayer, miracles, signs and wonders.\n\nMay 5\nS- Then He said to them, \"Follow Me and I will make you fishers of men\". Matt 4:19\n\nO- Follow me- keep, I will make- Work.- He said to them- fellowship, follow me, Fish for lost- Definition of Discipleship\n\nA- To have relationship! To be Armed- Fish Gr lost, Fellowship w( Believe Follow Jesus.\n\nP- God help me to be a disciple and to make disciples.",
