          "ocr_text": "April 24\nS- I have hope in God which they themselves also accept that there will be a resurrection of the dead both of the just and unjust. This being so I myself always strive to have a conscience without offense toward God and men. Acts 24:15\n\nO- There is going to be a day of account of everything known and unknown and a stricter judgement for those in authority.\n\nA- I need to live in a way that pleases God. In everything I do, see, think and act.\n\nP- God help me to love you more than everything in my life.\n\nApril 25\nS- Then Agrippa said to Festus, \"I also would like to hear the man myself.\" Tomorrow\" he said \"you shall hear him\". Acts 25:22\n\nO- Paul talking about Jesus resurrecting from the dead created so much hatred and tumult in the cities that it reached the ears of Agrippa. Pauls trial must be confiscated documented.\n\nA- I'll look up evidences of this trial in Roman history to see if there is record.\n\nP- This death of Paul is also proof of the resurrection of Christ. God please help me to die to myself the way that others have died for the gospel.\n\nApril 26\nS- Why should it be thought incredible to you that God raises the dead? Acts 26:8\n\nO- When speaking of hope of the promise that this hope motivated them to serve God night and day. This hope was hope of resurrection \u0026 a Messianic \u0026 saint.\n\nA- When I truly believe and have a hope in resurrection it will affect the way that I live and serve the Lord. I have love and an inheritance\n\nP- God help me to love and obey You. Hoping for resurrection",
