          "ocr_text": "Feb 27\nS- Do not worry about tomorrow. For you do not know what a\nday may bring forth. Prov 27:1\n\nO- We never know what will happen tomorrow so do now\nwhat I know is pleasing to God now.\n\nA- I will look at each moment as a opportunity to love\nthe Lord and to follow His commands. Tomorrow\nis never promised to anyone.\n\nP- Lord help me to live every moment as if it could\nbe the last time that I have to praise you.\n\n\nFeb 28\nS- Better is the poor who walks in his integrity than one\nperverse in his ways though he be rich. Prov 28:6\n\nO- Riches don't make my ways excuseable. It's better\nif I don't have wealth but I walk in integrity.\n\nA- I wont put my life on hold waiting to make money.\nI'm getting older. I need to take care of my\nspirit, soul and body.\n\nP- Good help me not to wait til I have money to\nserve you and trust you with my whole heart.\n\n\nMarch 1\nS- To give prudence to the simple, to the young man knowledge\nand discretion. Prov 1:4\n\nO- These proverbs can help me if I came to the Word as\na young man who is eager to learn and obey.\n\nA- I will come to the Word as a student and a learner\nand not as a teacher.\n\nP- God thank you for believing in me and trusting\nin me. to be a person that helps others\nbut help me never to forget that I need transformation\nfirst.",
