        {
          "created_at": "2026-06-17T02:35:33.438555+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "fceb5444-11a5-4c09-a0d0-106994cac14c",
          "import_batch_id": null,
          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2026-02-21",
          "ocr_text": "Feb 21\nS - The house is prepared for the day \u0026 battles beat oblivion.\n\u0026 Open the cloud. Prov. 21:31\n\nO - We can do all we want to prepare or not prepare but\nultimately God has the final say.\n\nA - I must appreciate and honor the Lord more.\nIt is the Lord that gives me all that I have.\nHe just needs to love and be loved by me.\n\nP - Oh help me to love you for you. I face others for\nothers but I love myself I you. Is a one\nwith everything\n\nPg 22\nS - Delusion is opening our eyes. Elisha servant - said\nGod's Reality.\nYou will reap a harvest if you do not faint. Gal.\nIf you are faithful everyday, you will be fruitful.\nA gap between our decisions \u0026 actions leads to future\nCompassionate Curiosity - I'm messed up. How can you fix me?\n\nG) Looks at my heart - My devotions should address our\nHeart. How is my heart? God is maturing when our heart\n\u0026 changes.\n\nLife is not a sprint. Its a marathon.\n\nI will never be fixed til glory\nWhy do I go from Moses to Julie mentality? Devotionals\n\u0026 Checklist - We turn our \"darlings\" on \u0026 off. Impatience\n\n2. Compartmentalism - Spiritual, carnal. I need to WALK in\nthe Spirit all the time.\n\n3. Performance - Devotions should lead to honesty in the\nway I live \u0026\nChrist is formed in you.\n\nCOMPASSIONATELY CURIOUS",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1781663732461.jpg",
