          "journal_date": "2026-02-16",
          "ocr_text": "Feb 16\nSo I heard discipline is for Him \u0026 unto Correction, this way, and he who hates correction will die. Prov 15:10\n\nO- Discipline is given to those that other follow. Hard discipline is given but I need to be corrected and dealt with. Cor 11:32. There is not a moment of rescue it.\n\nA- His goal is offer my neck and use chains and accept the discipline of the Lord.\n\nP- Lord please help me to receive discipline from you and that can away from it.\n\nFeb 11\nS- Commit your ways to the Lord and your thoughts will be established. Prov 16:3\n\nO- There is a connection between our hands and one head. Commit the works on our hands He will establish our thoughts.\n\nA- Many times I felt need to understand be for I work but I can leave that Be work to do and it will clear my mind.\n\nP- God I give you all the works of my hands. Please take everything that I do and use it to establish my hearts/thoughts\n\nFeb 11\nS- Rebuke is more effective for a wise man than 100 blows for a fool. Prov 17:10\n\nO- I don't need to suffer to learn if I am wise. I can learn from the rebuke of the Lord instead of discipline.\n\nA- I will be more receptive to hear and receive words from you through your word that to be corrected through pain. Help me to listen instead of being led through a bit an bridle.\n\nP- I will listen to your word and make time to treasure your voice. You want to speak to me not just discipline.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
