          "journal_date": "2026-01-17",
          "ocr_text": "Jan 17.\nS- And Jacob saw the countenance of Laban and indeed it was not favorable toward him as before Genesis 31/2\n\nO- When favor turns, it may be a sign that it's time to make a change w/ brothers. Pharah, who didn't know Joseph, and a lack of favor means its time to leave.\n\nA- When I don't get along with others, God is or could be signalling me to move on.\n\nP- God thank you that you are always in control of my life and my path. No matter who I have favor with or not.\n\nJan 16\nS- Laban called it segar sahadatha but Jacob called it Galed Gen 31:47\n\nO- segar - heap Sahadatha- witness. Language is Aramaic Galed - heap of witness - Hebrew. unity without uniformity. I meant the same thing spoken in 2 tongues. with ad as a witness between the 2 men.\n\nA- Laben later would produce some of the gentiles that spoke another language grafted into the kingdom through faith in Jesus Christ. Good events all people in His kingdom. Of all faiths. All tongues. All tribes. All nations.\n\nP- God please use me and my family to reach the nations of the world for your kingdom and for your glory.\n\nJan 19\nS- No one sews a piece of unshunk cloth on an old garment or else the new piece pulls away from the old, and the tear is made worse. Mark2:21\n\nO- Fasting is advised and explained as something that screws our minds to handle new truths. The key to stretch. Also it serves me. Not vice versa.\n\nA- I will try by the grace of God to practice fasting more.\n\nP- God please let this year be a year that practices fasting more, stretch my capacity and comprehension.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1781663924650.jpg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1781663924650.jpg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Genesis 31:2, Mark 2:21",
          "source": "manual",
          "summary": null,
