        {
          "created_at": "2026-06-17T02:39:19.318979+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "cca808d1-6632-438c-864a-bf6abcae6565",
          "import_batch_id": null,
          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2026-01-13",
          "ocr_text": "Jan 13\nS- And this stone which I have set as a pillar shall be God's house and of all that you give me I will surely give a tenth to you. Gen 28:22\n\nO- Abraham gives a tenth, Jacob gives a tenth. Isaac gives his tithe. Is there a place where a tenth is mentioned in the OT?\n\nA- I will give 10% of everything that God gives me back to him.\n\nP- God please give me a harvest and I will give a tenth of everything to you.\n\nJan 14\nS- So Jacob served seven yrs for Rachel and they only seemed like a few days because of the love that he had for her. Gen 29:20\n\nO- A mans love for a woman can get him to do an incredible amount of work for her. To give up his life. And it will seem effortless to him. The desire a man has toward a woman hold a lot of latent energy. Energy to make Ths seem like only days. Where does this energy go when rejected in a marriage. It goes to a lot of wrong places. A woman does not understand this. And a lot of destruction happens in a relationship because of this.\n\nA- How can this be explained? God knew this was going to change for me. And God warned me. That was a sad night for me.\n\nP- God thank you for taking me through that season. I wish it was shorter. I wish I had the courage to talk many years ago. God help me to redeem time.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1781663958699.jpg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1781663958699.jpg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Genesis 28:22, Genesis 29:20",
          "source": "manual",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-06-17T02:39:27.366+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-06-17T23:12:25.375188+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "date_reviewed": false,
          "id": "0be4e3d0-feb5-4b1d-bb7f-ef869ca556f6",
          "import_batch_id": null,
          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2026-06-12",
          "ocr_text": "“And in him you too are being built together to become a dwelling in which God lives by his Spirit.”\n‭‭Ephesians‬ ‭2‬:‭22‬ ‭NIV‬‬\nhttps://bible.com/bible/111/eph.2.22.NIV\n\nO- We are being built together to be a dwelling place for God. We all have something to contribute to one another. \n\nA- I will live in a way to understand what God is doing in the lives of others and to share their experiences so that we can all be encouraged by the good that God is doing in everyone’s life as we become Hos dwelling place. \n\nP- God thank you for living in us and through us to one another. Please help us not to live in silos but in community. To share one another’s victories and defeats and to lift each other up when we are discouraged and to humble one another when we are proud. Help us to put you first in the way we live.",
