          "journal_date": "2026-06-14",
          "ocr_text": "```json\n{\n  \"ocr_text\": \"June 12\\nS- And Moses indeed was faithful in all his house as a servant\\nfor a testimony of those things which would be spoken afterward,\\nbut Christ as Son over His own house, whose house we\\nare if we hold fast to the confidence and the rejoicing\\nof the hope firm to the end. Hebrews 3:5,6\\n\\nO- Moses was faithful to his house. Jesus was and is faithful to\\nHis house that I'm a part of. He will help me to be faithful\\nto the house He has given me to steward.\\n\\nA- I will work to steward every life that walks through the\\ndoors of my life and SBC.\\n\\nP- God thank you for helping me to steward the lives that\\nwalk in through the doors of the house. You were faithful.\\nHelp me to be faithful as well.\\n\\nJune 13\\nS- Let us there come boldly into the throne of grace that we\\nmay find grace to help in time of need. Hebrews 4:16\\n\\nO- There is a throne of grace now and a throne of judgment\\nlater. Everyone will gather involuntarily at the throne\\nof judgement later. But those spared will gather at the throne\\nof grace now.\\n\\nA- I will take time each day to begin my day at\\nthe throne of grace to find mercy and grace in time\\nof need.\\n\\nP- God please help me to understand there is a place\\nof authority where I can find mercy and grace and\\nto come boldly into that area. Joseph \u0026 Brothers\\n\\nJune 14\\nS- Though He was a son yet He learned obedience by the things\\nHe suffered. And having been perfected, He became the\\nauthor of eternal salvation to all who obey Him. Heb 5:8\\n\\nO- Suffering teaches obedience and results in perfection.\\nJesus being human needed to go through a process\\nlike us. Suffering → Obedience → Perfection.\\n\\nA- I must welcome suffering in my life to learn obedience\\nthat results in perfection.\\n\\nP- Lord help me to grow in my obedience and perfectio\",\n  \"scripture_reference\": \"Hebrews 3:5,6; Hebrews 4:16; Hebrews 5:8\"\n}\n```",
