          "journal_date": "2026-06-03",
          "ocr_text": "```json\n{\n  \"ocr_text\": \"June 3\\nS- So husbands ought to love their own wives as their own bodies. he that loves his wife loves himself. [C. For no one has hated his own flesh but nourishes and cherishes it just as the Lord does the church. Eph 5:28,29\\n\\nO- How did Jesus nourish his disciples? Judas was the treasurer. They had funds. When the woman gave to Jesus the disciples said 'why waste given away. Priority of poor was established. Their needs were taken care of. Jesus' responsibility to meet their needs and He did.\\n\\nA- It is my job to provide for my wife and my family. Not the church. Not James. Not anyone else but me. I need to do everything I can to provide for my wife and my kids.\\n\\nP- God please enable me to provide for Jose and the children you blessed me with.\\n\\nJune 4\\nS- Praying always with all prayer and supplication in the Spirit being watchful to this end with all perseverance and supplication for all saints, EP 6:18\\n\\nO- ALL PRAYER in the Spirit being watchful- Persevere in prayer.\\n\\nA- I need to be prayerful and the Spirit will give me eyes to see.\\n\\nP- God thank you for blessing me and loving me. Help me to pray and be watchful.\\n\\nJune 5\\nS- Take the helmet of salvation, and the sword of the Spirit which is the word of God. Eph 6:17\\n\\nO- The Word isn't our sword, but the Spirit's sword. I give the Spirit something to use in my life when I read the Word.\\n\\nA- I will read continuously, so the Spirit can cut my heart and work into my life.\\n\\nP- God many times I need the Word of God to cut into my heart and life. The Word of God doesn't have a handle.\",\n  \"scripture_reference\": \"Ephesians 5:28-29, Ephesians 6:18, Ephesians 6:17\"\n}\n```",
