          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2026-05-29",
          "ocr_text": "O- Paul is stating how previous ages didn't understand God's plan in saving the Gentiles. Now that Gentiles are saved many don't think God will save the Jews. God Paul says salvation is for the Gentiles in Ephesians and for the Jews in Hebrew. Salvation is for all who God calls to unite humanity in Jesus. Through Jesus by the spirit to the father.\n\nA- When I start thinking salvation is only for me I miss the heart of Jesus to unite humanity in Christ. He's the same. If I understand His plan to save humanity by the spirit, through Christ, to the father, I can participate in God's mission. Gentiles repent of sin to follow Christ. Gentiles' repent of rightousness to follow Christ. Christians repent of both.\n\nP- God thank you that we can know your ways by reading your Word and understanding your intention through the Spirit, through Jesus. Help me to be a peacemaker.\n\nMay. 29\nS- ...that I should preach among the Gentiles the unsearchable riches of Christ, and to make all see what is the fellowship of the mystery which from the beginning of the ages has been hidden in God who created all things through Jesus Christ, to the intent that now the manifold wisdom of God might be made known by the church to the principalities and powers in heavenly places according to the eternal purpose which He accomplished in Christ Jesus our Lord. Eph 3: 8-11\n\nO- Paul's mission was to share the mystery of Christ to the Gentiles as the creator of all and that mystery would be shown to principalities and powers according to the eternal purpose accomplished in Christ.\n\nA- The church will make known to the principalities and powers in heavenly places what Christ has accomplished.\n\nP- God help me to understand this mystery. It's not about doing. It's about being. And being is about knowing. Knowing truth allows me to be. Help me to know so I can be and out of being I will do.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
