          "ocr_text": "A- I will see that only Jesus paved a is the way, by the Spirit. Father, Jesus is the only way that fulfills the Spirit is Jesus is available to me as much as anyone else. We just I get to God, the more distance I fall with those who are not living according to those standards. My righteousness becomes a wall to those on the other side. God wants me to love like Jesus without partaking of sin. The more I dislike the left, the more I rely on my own righteousness. The more I love Jesus, the more I die. I would HATE sin because that is what Christ died to cleanse, but the more I should love the sinner, because its that love for the sinner that drove Christ to the cross.\n\nP- Jesus thank you for you love for me that drove you to the cross. Thank you for living a perfect life and for coming here to model what perfection looks like in a broken world. Thank you that you sacrificed your life to atone for my sin. Thank you for sending your Spirit to show us the way to the Father. Thank you that you call me to bring unity to all those who are walking contrary to you by loving them and paying for their sins as well. I need to lay down my righteous view and pick up Jesus. They need to lay down sin and pick up Jesus. If we all pick up Jesus, we will find unity and peace on earth. If we hold on to sin, we reject Jesus. If we hold on the self righteousness, we reject Jesus. It is only through Jesus, by the Spirit to the Father. Please continue to hold me Jesus. Spirit teach me about Jesus and lead me to the Father. Amen.\n\nv 28\nFor this reason I Paul the prisoner of Christ Jesus for you gentiles, if indeed you heard of the dispensation of the grace of God which was given to me for you, how that by revelation He made known to me the mystery (as I have briefly written already by which, when you read, you may understand my knowledge in the mystery of Christ), which in other ages was not made known to the sons of men, as now has been revealed by the Spirit to His holy apostles and prophets, that the gentiles should be fellow heirs of the same body, and partakers of His promise in Christ through the gospel of which I became a minister according to the gift of the grace of God given to me by the effective working of His power. Eph 3: 1-7",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
