          "ocr_text": "May 26\nS- And he put all things under His feet and gave Him to be the head over all things to the church which is His body, the fullness of Him who fills all in all. Eph. 1:22,23\n\nO- All authority has been given to Jesus and He now gives that authority to the church which is His body. The fullness of Him. He is the one who baptizes with love. He put authority to lead and make disciples.\n\nA- I need to abide in and with Jesus if I want to be fruitful. I need to eliminate distractions. Burn my boats. Separate myself from disorders. Focus on His word and making disciples.\n\nP- God I'm sorry for my wasted years of not pursuing you with my whole heart. Help me to love you first and love and provide for my family the way you provide for me. You have been so faithful to me through the years. Help me to live for you till I die. I'm not worthy but grant me the gift of resurrection.\n\nMay 27\nS- For He Himself is our peace who has made both one and has broken down the middle wall of separation having abolished in His flesh the enmity that is, the law of commandments contained in the ordinances, so as to create in Himself one new man from the two, thus making peace, and that He might reconcile them both to God in one body through the cross thereby putting to death the enmity. And He came and preached peace to you who were afar off and to those who were near, for through Him we both have access by one Spirit to the Father. Eph 2:14-16\n\nO- Commands were made to bring Jews to God. Commands that came to provide a way separated Jews from Gentiles. Jesus body. Commands couldn't get Jews to God because they couldn't fulfill it. So Christ fulfilled the perfect law. Then died as a sacrifice to take upon Himself the sins not only of Jews but Gentiles as well. The sacrifice satisfied sin and transgressions for all. Jews need to have humility to see their work isn't good enough and that Jesus is better. Gentiles need humility to repent from their ways and to follow the way of Christ that through Christ we are empowered by the Spirit to access the Father. The Father's heart was unity with Himself and all of humanity through Jesus His Son and unity all humanity through Jesus His Son. \"That they might be one as we are one.\"",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
