          "ocr_text": "April 4\nS- all things work together for good to those who love God and are called according to His purpose. I think of those who are the called according to His purpose.\n\nO- all things are not good, but all things work together. A good is we are called according to His purpose.\n\nA- I should live in assurance that I am part of the called according to His purpose and He will dwell in all the plans of redemption, where this corrupted body will put on incorruption.\n\nP- God please help me to walk out my call in Jesus and developing knowing you are a counseling fire.\n\nApril 5th\nS- for other, he foreknew. He also predestined to be conformed to the image of God His son that He might be the firstborn of many brethren. Rom 8:29.\n\nO- He will one day look like Christ. The Resurrected Christ. The sin of the corruptible made incorruptible. If we die like Him we will rise like Him.\n\nA- I need to live in a way that is, like Christ in public and in private. It's the way I die that will determine the way I rise. It's the way I live that will determine the way I die. It's the way I die that will determine how I rise.\n\nP- God help me to live worthy of a death that is rewarded by resurrection.\n\nApril 6th\nS- Why? Because they did not seek righteousness by faith but as it were by the works of the law. they stumbled at the stumbling stone. Rom 9:32\n\nO- God chose gentiles over Jews even though Jews pursued righteousness because gentiles pursued Jews pursued righteousness through the law. While\n\nA- I can get righteousness if I seek if through faith in Christ and not my works.\n\nP- God help me to trust in your love and expel grace for my life and not my works. But my off all sin because I'm blessed",
