          "ocr_text": "May 12\nS- For he was a good man, full of the Holy Spirit and of faith\nand a great many people were added to the Lord. Act 11:24\n\nO- Barnabas was described as full of the Holy Spirit and many\npeople were added. The word added is interesting. Not led. But\nwon. But added. This implies it was a work of God and\nnot Barnabas\n\nA- Most focus on doing instead of being. As Barnabas focused\non being God added many to the faith. Gods main desire\nis that I'm fruitful to the vine and He will\ngive me fruit and multiply me.\n\nP- God help me to abide in you. Fill me w/ your spirit so\nI have the fruits of the spirit.\n\nMay 13\nS- The Lord detests the way of the wicked but He loves those\nwho pursue righteousness. Stern discipline awaits anyone\nwho leaves the way/path. The one who hate correction\nwill die. Prov 15; 9,10\n\nO- Righteousness doesn't just happen. Doesn't just fall in someones\nlap. If someone wasn't righteousness it need to be pursued.\nLike a spouse, treasure, deer. It takes a tremendous amount\nof effort. God loves to see men pursue it. Discipline\nis the mark of being a son. Embrace discipline and love.\n\nA- I will give thought to the effort I need to place in\nmy life to live rightly before the Lord. We wages\nare before Him and He notices the effort.\n\nP- God help me not to run from feelings of conviction but\nto embrace it as your approval and love for my life. Thank\nyou for nothing is hidden from your view and all\neffect is noticed by you.\n\nMay 14\nS- So they said \"Believe in the Lord Jesus Christ and you will\nbe saved, you and your house hold. Then they spoke the word of\nthe Lord to him and all who were in his house. And heard of\nthem the same hour of the night and washed their feet.\nAnd immediately he and all his family were baptized. Now\nwhen he had brought them into his house he set food\nbefore them and rejoiced having believed in God\nw/ his household. Act 16; 31-34",
