          "ocr_text": "O- Salvation of household followed his true belief. His belief was shown through a 180° change in action. The word was spoken to his entire family. The jailer strips. The act of repentance of the jailer led the family getting baptized.\n\nA- When someone gets saved attention should be given to their home and family members. Attention should be paid to true repentance. Repentance looks different for different people. Peter stopped zagging gave money back. How can I continue to repent belief in the gospel demands action.\n\nP- God help me to continue to grow in you to change my actions, to be aware of others changing their actions and focusing on families not just individuals coming to you.\n\nMay 15\n\nS- Then after some days Paul said to Barnabas let us go back and visit our brethren in every city where we have preached the word of the Lord and see how they are doing. Act 15:36\n\nO- Paul didn't just preach but he went back to check on those who received his word and were baptized.\n\nA- When people are baptized and added to the family of God, I should regularly check in on them to see how they have doing.\n\nP- God help me to have a shepherds heart and to share the gospel of the kingdom to everyone I come in contact with.\n\nMay 16\n\nS- Now a certain woman named Lydia heard us. She was a seller of purple from Thyatira who worshipped God. The Lord opened her heart to hear the things spoken by Paul. And when she and her household were baptized she begged us saying \"If you have judged me to be faithful to the Lord, come to my house and stay so\" she persuaded us. Acts 16:15,16\n\nO- Lots of thought given to details. Seller of purple from Thyatira. Worshipper of God. Heart of hospitality. This was a person of peace. They went to who the Lord was calling. In the she peace",
