          "ocr_text": "May 4.\nS- 'And He spoke boldly in the name of the Lord and disputed with the Hellenists but they attempted to kill him. Acts\n\nO- This was the pattern in Acts and today with Charlie Kirk. Truth can always stand without violence. It's something true it can stand in any words. People who believe lies will resort to violence when they can't win a debate.\n\nA- They killed Jesus, Peter, Paul, Charlie. I should not arm myself with guns and weapons but with facts. Jesus was actually deeply political and was killed because of the truth that he was the true king of the Jews.\n\nP- God help me to know the truth and have the courage to speak it even if people get upset.\n\nMay 10\nS- And He commanded us to preach to the people and to testify that it is he, who was ordained by God to judge of the living and the dead. To Him all the prophets witness that through His name, whoever believes in Him will receive remission of sins. Acts 10:42,43\n\nO- We are to preach forgiveness of sins through Jesus but also Jesus as Judge. He forgives but will judge as well.\n\nA- God help me to understand the fear of the Lord. To walk in the Spirit. To have a hatred of sin.\n\nP- I will pray for the Spirit to fill me to walk in Him so I won't fulfill the lust of the flesh.\n\nMay 11\nS- You went to the uncircumcised non and ate with them But Peter explained it to them in order from the beginning saying I was in Joppa Acts 11:3-16\n\nO- All through Acts the apostles encountered God and gave them direction they followed their explained that encounter and direction from the Spirit.\n\nA- I need to seek the Spirits direction first, at second, explain third\n\nP- God please lead and guide me in all my ways. Help me to be obedient in all things. To follow you first, obey second and speak last.",
