          "ocr_text": "April 10\nS- And when he observed him, he was afraid and said 'What is this?' and he said to him, 'Your prayers and your alms have come up for a memorial before God.' Acts 10:4\n\nO- God remembered this man's prayers and generosity to the poor. God sees and remembers all.\n\nA- Everything I do or don't do is given and rewarded by God. I must be faithful to the call that God has on my life.\n\nP- God help me to not be lazy or unfaithful w/ the call you have for me. I want to live like David not Samson.\n\nApril 11\nS- When they heard these things they became silent and they glorified God saying 'Then God has also granted to the gentiles repentance to life.' Acts 11:18\n\nO- The Jews response to Gentiles being filled w/ the Holy Spirit and being baptized was they were granted repentance to life. Repentance was a gift that led to life.\n\nA- I need to live in a way that pleases God so He will grant me repentance to life and not death\n\nP- God, help me to live and walk in the Spirit and not in the flesh.\n\nApril 12\nS- But the word of God grew and multiplied. Acts 12:24\n\nO- In spite of persecution, the Word of God multiplied and grew.\n\nA- God's Word grows when His people speak it to another and it changes and transforms people's lives. Even persecution cannot stop God's word from changing and transforming lives.\n\nP- If I spend time in God's word it will change me. As it changes me I can share how it did that to others and it will grow and multiply through my life.",
