          "journal_date": "2026-03-22",
          "ocr_text": "March 22\nS- And says Here saying to me, 'Make haste and get out of Jerusalem. Because thy stay here is not necessary concerning me they that believed in you. And then the blood of a Russian your martyr's will is standing by consenting to his death and clothing him. Then he said to me 'Depart for I will send you far away hence to the gentiles.' And they listened to him until this word and then they raised their voices and said, 'Away with such a fellow from the earth for he is not fit to live!' Acts 22:18-23\n\nO- Even in sharing his testimony, they still wanted to kill him because that way, law, place, customs were being threatened. They loved these things more than Jesus. More than truth.\n\nA- Sometimes truth will threaten a person's way of life. When they love their way of life more than Jesus/Truth, they will hate you.\n\nP- God please help me to love truth and Jesus more than my own way of living. You invite me to come and die. Die to my ways. Die for your love of others. Fill me with your love.\n\nMarch 23\nS- But when Paul perceived that one part were Sadducees and another Pharisees he cried out in the council 'Men and brethren, I am a Pharisee, the son of a Pharisee, concerning the hope and resurrection of the dead I am being judged!' And when he said this a dissension arose between the Pharisees and Sadducees and the assembly concluded. Acts 23:6\n\nO- A kingdom divided against itself cannot stand. After Paul was in the assembly, he divided the assembly using the difference of their held beliefs. Later a group of 40 united around the goal to kill him. So God gave him a united group of over 200 guards to protect him. 270 to 5+10guards.\n\nA- A united group of people with a clear mission will be very difficult to stop. Focusing on differences will stop any group from uniting.\n\nP- God, thank you for giving me authority to make disciples. Help me to walk with you to do it.",
