          "ocr_text": "March 29\n\nAs His divine power has given to us all things that pertain to life and godliness, through the knowledge of him that hath called us to glory and virtue, by which have been given unto us exceeding great and precious promises, that through these ye might be partakers of the divine nature, having escaped the corruption that is in the world through lust. II Peter 1:3,4\n\nO - God has given everything that pertains to life and godliness through the knowledge of him who called us by glory and virtue by which we have been given exceedingly great and precious promises. I may be partaker of the divine nature having escaped the corruption that is in the world through lust.\n\nA- God has divine power has given us everything that pertains to life and godliness through the knowledge of him who called us by glory and virtue.\n\nP- God has given me everything that pertains to life and godliness through the knowledge of him who called us in glory and virtue\n\nPalm Sunday\nExodus 12: 5,6,7,12,13,14\nJohn 12: 12-1,12\n1500yrs - Jews celebrated passover, selecting their lambs to slaughter\nII Peter 2:8, B 10:9 + loaye = 1 day\nGen 5:11 Matt 1-1 2000yr adam→Abraham, 2000yr Abraham→Jesus\n4000yr Adam → Jesus\n\nMarch 30\nS- Now after the piece of bread Satan entered him. Then Jesus said to him \"what you do, do quickly\". John 13:27\n\nD- Communion didn't save Judas from his sin. In fact it accelerated the hardness. He needed to repent to sin. Jesus didn't stop him but encouraged him to do it quickly. Why? Paul explains why so many unworthily are sick is because they partake of the body in an unworthy manner. I'm a selfless manner. The broken body was made for the selfless and the grateful! I wasn't made for the ungrateful, and selfish. Do it quickly. So an cold. For the ungrateful, and selfish. Do it quickly. So an cold. Make a decision and stick with it. God for the body will happen no matter what. Jesus was concerned for the decision to be made so evil could be used as good for the body. Not for Judas'\n\nA- I should make decisions swiftly to honor God and repent of sin\nP- God help me to be decisive in good choices.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
