          "ocr_text": "march 24\nS- Now he reasoned about righteousness, self control and judgment were to come. He felt was afraid for me. I felt like I should have told him about righteousness for then when I have a convenient time. I must keep telling him about Jesus.\n\nO- Paul had things interesting to tell to hear. Righteousness, self control, judgement were things that only he at his conveyances. He wasn't ready to change his life and repent. He had his own way about what was right, the ability and self control. He wasn't ready to repent.\n\nA- I should be aware of when someone is listening out of convenience and when they are willing to repent and change their way.\n\nP- God help me to be willing to change in ways, to repent and follow you in what is righteous, what ways I need self control and what I will be judged for.\n\nmarch 25\nS- When the accusers stood up they brought no accusation against him of such things as I supposed but had some questions against him about their own religion and about a certain man Jesus who had died whom Paul affirmed to be alive. Acts 25:16,17\n\nO- The hostility against Paul was around the resurrection of Jesus and hope it offered. The truth was key to the point of death. He was interested even the highest leaders, at all. He judged in righteousness and had interest of eternal life and willingly.\n\nA- The truth will disrupt our lives. It disrupted the Jews. It disrupted the gentiles. It disrupted the Kings. It should disrupt me.\n\nP- God help me to repent of sin, righteousness and judgment. Help me to repent of what the Bible calls sin. Help me to live my life in a way that adheres to what you say is righteous. Aid to live in a way that is worthy of judgement.",
