          "ocr_text": "March 17\nS- Paul was always in the synagogue. Christ in every city. Teaching about Jesus and the resurrection. Here were some prominent businessmen then believed (Thessalonians - place of resurrection) Then he was chased out and went to Athens. They studied and be listened. (12 many women) received Him always a only wanted to hear of Jesus and the new. A Paul modeled on - Chapter 17 as received. Others just tolerated. Paul modeled on - Chapter 17\n\nO- Paul had a place and time to spread the gospel. Place-synagogue marketplace and the audience - Influential marketplace leaders Message. Jesus \u0026 Resurrection.\n\nA- I need a place, time, taught audience, message. I'm very scattered in all these things because I allow the fatigo to dictate much of my activities out. I need to give my shoulder and focus to the Lord.\n\nP- God help me to give my focus and att\n\nMarch 18\nS- So because of the he was of the same trade he stayed with them and worked for by occupation they were tentmakers. And he reasoned in the synagogue every sabbath and persuaded both Jews and Greeks. Acts 18:3,4\n\nO- This is a great example of what Jesus taught in Luke 10. Find a man of peace, stay in a house and work and eat what is set before you.\n\nA- I should look for common interest to begin to share the Word and make disciples. Paul stayed in Corinth for 1½ 18\n\nP- God help me to be sensitive to your Spirit, follow Luke 10 and make disciples.\n\nMarch 19\nS- Interesting that in Act 19 12 of Johns disciples were baptized in the Holy Spirit as Paul continued to preach everyday for 3 months then continued for 2 more years. God confirmed what he was saying with signs and wonders. There are many that opposed what he was saying but Pauls word prevailed when he returned to Ephesus.\n\nO- Word declared in the marketplace. Contended by God through answered prayers. Contended by others but contended by God through answered prayers.\n\nA- If we had to see miracles we should preach and expect contention the Word to be proved and to prevail\n\nP- God help me to be diligent to sharing you with others.",
