          "ocr_text": "March 17\nS- And when he saw it pleased give Jesus he proceeded further \u0026 seize Peter also. Was it during the last @ unleashed bread Act 12:3\n\nO- Herod did things because it pleased the people so he didn't lead again, he was lead by them. You can't lead people if you need people\n\nA- I must serve people by leading them well. Not by doing things to please them or things they want but by how the word describes a good leader.\n\nP- God, help me to lead well. I had a baseline of my dreams \u0026 get dialed in to what you have for us.\n\nMarch 18\nS- Process - Jesus had a practice of listening \u0026 sharing the Word. They used that platform and combined their history with the present \u0026 the future promise. This produced a foundation for them to know the gospel but Jesus kept the word from spreading. None of these things were required for gentiles to receive gospel.\nB- Now when gentiles heard this they were glad and gloried the word of the Lord. And as had been appointed to eternal life believed. Acts 13:48\n\nO- Jesus had practice of hearing \u0026 discussing the word. They heard scripture, they knew about past (history)-future. The gentiles heard and received because it was a line. Jesus wanted both old and new preserved. The Old needed the New but the New also needed the depth and foundation at the old.\n\nA- God will pour out the Spirit to whom he will best we must befaithful to share and connect the old with the new\n\nP- God please help me to, lift my eyes to see the harvest of the old and the new and to connect the generations to walk in what you have for them\n\nhello this pen is\nco thin. Love you! -Mom",
