          "ocr_text": "March 6\nS= When you were they will lead you, when you sleep they will keep you, and when you awaken, they will speak with you. Proverbs 3:24\n\nO= The commands of God guide us, protect us, and speak to us. The commands of God have a positive benefit, it'd work when we are at rest.\n\nA= It is well memorized that commands of God, it will continuously work in my life, whether I'm working sleeping, waking, His word will work in our life.\n\nP= God help me to be more faithful in my time for your word.\n\nMarch 7\nS= But when the time of promise drew near which God had sworn to Abraham the people grew and multiplied in Egypt. It scattered being worst who did yo't obey Joseph. Acts 7:17,18.\n\nO= God commanded Abraham to be the father of many nations. It happened through one son. God took His people in Egypt as a blessing that turned into a curse.\n\nA= Gods plan will always come to pass. It will take more time with patience. Wonders the purpose but God will always achieve His purpose in my life and the lives is those he calls.\n\nP= God help me to be patient and faithful to your voice and your warnings to me. Help me to hate sin with all my heart.\n\nMarch 4\nS= Then Simon answered and said, I agree to it, be that none of the things which ye have spoken may come upon me. Acts 8:24\n\nO= Simon was baptized, saved and believed and even he was cursed because he desired to buy the holy spirit.\n\nA= Maybe we shouldn't pair the kids to do their souls.\n\nP= God help me to be able to motivate one kids to allow them many you and your word will draw them money.",
