          "ocr_text": "March 2\nS- For you dear teacher, as elder and search for her/as a child instructs that you call understand the fear of the lord. God said, Blessed are those who fear him; Blessed are the Lord. True wisdom begins knowledge; Psalm 111:10 and understanding is about you all around wisdom for the upright We is a shield to those who walk uprightly. Prov 2:7-8\n\nO- Fear of the Lord is something that most people don't understand because they don't correct for mistakes. For of the Lord is something that is comforting for most people bc fear is anything that is correcting us. Rather than running away from it, we should let the Lord that he is good and can only be understood and experienced by someone seeking Wisdom.\n\nA- I need to continue seeking wisdom. I need to deliver from the innate woman. Those going to death, many never repain deliverance til I'm delivered. Deliverance is a by product of pursuing Wisdom.\n\nP- God give us grace to pursue you with my whole heart. You must so much more! Lord help us and especially lived to come the lost to be got distracted by worldless things.\n\nMarch 3\nS- My son do not forget my law. But let your heart keep my commands. For length of days and long life and peace, they will add to you. Let not mercy and truth forsake you. Bind them around your neck. Write them on the tablet of your heart. And so favor with God and man. Prov 3:1-4\n\nO- Embrace the statues of mercy and truth. This give you favor with men and also from the sinner. Walking is truth yield mercy for thyself\n\nA- I need to strive to have a perfect walk with mercy for myself when I fails, then. Lifting up others I can do this by remembering the commands of God And Keeping them.\n\nP- God help me to seek you first with my whole heart and to stop to hear your voice throughout the day. Help me to walk out your commands and to remember both mercy and truth in my own life.",
