          "ocr_text": "Feb 12\nS- An excellent wife is the crown of her husband. But she who causes shame to life rotteness in his bones. Prov 12:4\n\nO- A wife can be a crown or rotteness of her bones. She is a crown as a crown of glory. A crown on the head of her king displays honor to a king but is also a spectacle of beauty, held up as a wife that dishonors a man remains unsan at birth, him as well\n\nA- A wife can make a man look like a king and I doing so lifts myself up. A women that degrades her husband degrades herself over rots her husband\n\nP- God thank you for an excellent amazing wife that honors me and makes herself beautiful and valuable for doing so.\n\nFeb 13\nS- Righteousness guards him whose walk is blameless But wickedness over throws the sinner Prov 13:6\n\nO- If my ways are righteous it will preserve me. If my ways are wicked, it will destroy me.\n\nA- My ways are either preserving or destroying me. I must chose offenders\n\nP- God, thank you that you have given me such a rich heritage and so many things that can help me walk in a way that is right to you and life giving to myself and for those around me.\n\nFeb 14\nS- The fear of the Lord is a fountain of life to turn one away from the snares of death. Prov 14:27\n\nO- The fear of the Lord will give me life and turn me away from many ways that I could die. There are many ways to die and one way to live to fear the Lord.\n\nA- I want to understand the fear of the Lord in a deeper way. I understand the grace of God but have not embraced the fear of the Lord.\n\nP- God please give me greater insight into fearing you and turning from evil. All your ways are for my good. Help me to love you, fear you.",
