          "ocr_text": "what there are when they had come together they asked him, saying, Lord, wilt thou at this time restore the kingdom to Israel? And he said unto them, It is not for you to know the times or the seasons, which the Father hath put in his own power. But ye shall receive power when the Holy Ghost is come upon you: and ye shall be witnesses unto me both in Jerusalem, and in all Judaea, and in Samaria, and unto the uttermost part of the earth. Acts 1:6-8\n\nO- They wanted an earthly kingdom, but in the Father's divine will, the Father calls rightful kingdom. You preach the gospel. Gospel of the Kingdom.\n\nA- My duty is the same as the apostles. To wait for the promise of the Spirit and obey the command to be a witness of Jesus. Help me to never be distracted by worry or wealth or any other thing. Help me to always be focused on sharing the gospel.\n\nbib\nS- And they were all filled with the Holy Spirit and began to speak of other tongues as the Spirit gave them utterance. Acts 2:4\n\nO- The Spirit gave them utterance. They were in one place waiting for 10 days. The Spirit inhabits those awaiting the promise.\n\nA- There needs to be a stillness in my life. Be still, know that I am God. I will be exalted among the heathen. I will be exalted in all the earth. The earth is the Lord's and the fullness thereof.\n\nP- God my mind is not in a good space. It's over stimulated. I need to be still. I need you in my life to overcome my sin. Please give me your peace.\n\nFeb 6\nS- He Crossing this spoke concerning the resurrection of the Christ, that his Soul was not left in Hades, nor did his flesh see corruption. Acts 2:31\n\nO- There were two parts of the death \u0026 resurrection. His soul and body. His soul was not left in hell. His body was not left in the grave.\n\nA- I can have a hope that if I die like Christ I can be resurrected like Him as well. To be w/ Jesus and resurrected.\n\nP- God help me to have my heart set on eternity",
