          "ocr_text": "Feb 3\nS- Do not be wise in your own eyes. Fear the Lord and depart from evil. It will be health to your flesh and strength to your bones. Prov 3: 7-8\n\nO- Humility is shown by changing the way I do things. When I'm humble and put God in his rightful place it will affect my physical body!\n\nA- God, I will change, by submitting myself into your hands to change my life.\n\nP- God thank you that you see me as a man of God and with humility, honor, and integrity. None of those things are true now. I ask you to transform my heart and life in Jesus name!\n\nFeb 4\nS- For the ways of man are before the Lord and he ponders all his paths. Prov 5: 21\n\nO- Proverbs encouraged me to ponder the path of my feet and that God himself ponders my path.\n\nA- Where am I? I ain far from the Lord. How do I get close again. What first works must I return to? How do I return to my first love?\n\nP- God please guide me back to you. I have drifted lost and far from you. Give me grace to return to your presence.\n\nFeb 5\nS- For Christ did not send me to baptize but to preach the gospel, not with wisdom of words, lest the cross of Christ should be made of no effect. I Cor 1: 17\n\nO- Paul had a clear directive to preach. Not even baptize but to preach. And within preaching- the taste to preach and the reason!\n\nA- I can always be more focused. 1) What I am not called to 2) What I'm called to 3) How I'm called to do it. 4) Purpose of why I need to do it that way\n\nP- God help me to focus on the call you have for my life. The way \u0026 purpose",
