          "ocr_text": "Jan 31\nS: Charm is deceitful and beauty is passing but a woman who fears\nthe Lord she shall be praised. Prov 31:30\n\nO: Charm and beauty are temporal but they is the core of\nthat makes a woman invaluable and keeper.\n\nA: I am thankful that God has given me a helpful wife who is a hard worker. She\nwhile who is a hard worker. I am grateful for my first and the\nlove I've been very blessed as a wife that knows\n\nP: Lord help me to treasure and honor Jocelyn and all the\nchildren that you gave blessed me with.\n\nFeb 1\nS: So are the ways of everyone who is greedy \u0026 gain.\nIt takes away the life of its owners. Prov 1:19\n\nO: People who are greedy do not cave about their own\nlives. Greed destroys life because it become\nconsumption, control, power, esteem \u0026 others.\nThese things are not life, seeking these things\ntake away from life.\n\nA: I must practice restraint and self discipline.\nSelf indulgence and cowardice will never satisfy\n\nP: God thank you for all that you have given to me\nhelp me to be a faithful steward of all you have given\n\nFeb 2\nS: The wicked will be cut off from the earth and\nthe unfaithful shall be uprooted from it. Prov 2:22\n\nO: Being on the earth is a promise to the righteous. Not\njust now but in the perspective of eternity. God\nhas promised for the faithful to dwell on the\nearth.\n\nA: The promise of eternal life is so much greater\nthan simple heaven after death but resurrection\nafter heaven on earth.\n\nP: God please help me to be focused on the promise\nof resurrection much more than heaven.",
