          "ocr_text": "Jan 27\nS- The Fear of the Lord is the beginning of knowledge and best fears despite wisdom and instruction. Prov 1:7\n\nO- Wisdom starts by honoring the Lord and wanting to do what he wants. Wisdom is not just a head knowledge but is accepting and bearing the consequences for it.\n\nA- I do fear God. I must realize that and continue to expose that and walk in that direction. I need to be in God and encourage myself in the Lord.\n\nP- God thank you that you love me and are pleased with me. Help me to look to you for you. Help as Allow me to let you speak to me as I write and accept your love and grace.\n\nJan 29\nS- Turn at my rebuke, Surely I will pour out my spirit on you. I will make my words known to you. Prov 1:23\n\nO- The promise of God is clear. If I listen to His correction He will draw near to me. He will help me understand wisdom and accept His word to me.\n\nA- God I will love me for God. I listen to His conviction because He loves me. I will draw near to Him this year. He is inviting me to Himself.\n\nP- God thank you that you constantly are moving toward us in love and invitations. Draw me close to you.\n\nJan 30\nS- Every Word of God is pure He is a shield to those who put their trust in him. Prov 30:5\n\nO- When I study the Word it will reveal the junk in my heart and allow me to purge my heart of evil. It be comes a shield to me a defense to my heart.\n\nA- I need to daily jump into scripture and allow God to chafe all edges in my heart that is wrong.\n\nP- God please continue to shape and mold my heart and life. It's so easy to be distracted by things unimportant and temporal instead of eternal.",
