          "ocr_text": "Jan 15\n6 When the Lord saw that Leah was unloved, He opened her womb\nbut Rachael was barren. Genesis 29:31\n\nO- God is our defender and loves us and blesses us when\nwe are unloved. It was sad also that\nSarah loved her more than God. Leah prayed for\nthat when she stopped focusing on the love of Jacobs and directed\nher praise to God\nchildren as if she was complete. Sarahs Judah\nbecame one of the most well known tribes of Israel.\n\nA- I should focus on Gods love for me, Not my lack\nof love from others. I will feel complete when my\neyes are on Christ and my praise is directed to Him.\n\nP- God help me to see you as my first love. Help me to\nunderstand you want to bless me because of your love\nfor me. Help me not to use your blessing to try\nto have another persons love. Help me\nto always love you more than people and stop and\npraise you for your blessings to me instead of\ntrying to earn love from those who will never\ncare.\n\nJan 16\nS- So the flocks conceived before the rods, and the flocks\nbrought forth streaked, speckled and spotted. Genesis 30:32\n\nO- Jacob was deceived into working 7 more years but Laban\ngave him 2 more wives and those whom gave Jacob\n12 sons. He was asked to stay for and look the\nvail spotted it but the spots didn't spot of their\nown. He wanted the strong. Jacob turned the\noffense into a blessing.\n\nA- In every situation, God can bless me. I shouldn't\nfocus on any offense but on God who is in\ncontrol as God who blesses.\n\nP- God thank you that in all situations you are my\ndefender and you are my provider so I can\nrely on you to take care of me.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
